livery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Changes in Job Detail View\nDescription: The job detail view has been revised. General information, originally repeated in the header, is now only displayed in the General Information section. As a result, the General Information section has moved to the top of the page, with details about the builds below.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-23\nValid as Of: 2024-09-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2236 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional Prerequisite for Task List Template Deletion\nDescription: The deletion of a task list template is now allowed only if no production task list exists that was created from the template less than ten years ago, independently of the task list's status. This validation supports you in adhering to audit-relevant retention times.  More information:  How to Delete Task List Templates and Task Lists  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-09\nValid as Of: 2024-09-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2237 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Upcoming Clean-Up and Future Deletion of Change Logs\nDescription: In one of the upcoming releases, a new system behavior will be implemented for the case of task list template or task list deletion. For compliance reasons, change logs relating to a task list template or task list that is being deleted, will then be deleted as well.  Additionally, for change logs relating to task list templates and task lists that have already been removed, a clean up will take place to ensure that these change logs are deleted.  App affected:  Change Log\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-09\nValid as Of: 2024-09-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2238 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Edge Integration Cell Runtime Update\nDescription: Edge Integration Cell now runs on Java 17.  See: Deploy the Edge Integration Cell Solution\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-21\nValid as Of: 2024-09-21\nVersion: 2408\n\n--- Record 2239 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Emergency Recovery is now supported\nDescription: You can now perform an emergency recovery for the Edge Integration Cell from scratch, in the event of a Kubernetes (K8s) cluster environment loss.  See: Perform Emergency Recovery\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-21\nValid as Of: 2024-09-21\nVersion: 2408\n\n--- Record 2240 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Thread Dump\",1330\n420,\"--- Record 1731 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Model library  Explore models available in generative AI hub and their metadata, using the catalog mode.   Inform your decision making using benchmarking data, using the leaderboard mode.   View detailed information for a single model such as data input types, cost information and metrics where available on its model card.  For more information, see Model Library.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-16\nValid as Of: 2024-12-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1732 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models and model versions from AWS Bedrock are supported.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-16\nValid as Of: 2024-12-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1733 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Developer's Guide\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Tutorials for Consuming Remote Services and Deploying in SAP BTP, Kyma Runtime Moved to Tutorial Navigator\nDescription: The tutorials that show how to integrate the SAP S/4HANA Cloud Business Partner API to the Incident Management application are now moved to the Tutorial Navigator. There are two main groups depending on whether you have an SAP S/4HANA Cloud tenant, or you use a mock server:       Consume Remote Services from S/4HANA Cloud in Your Full-Stack CAP Application Following the SAP BTP Developer's Guide and Deploy in SAP BTP, Kyma Runtime      Consume Remote Services from a Mock Server in Your Full-Stack CAP Application Following the SAP BTP Developer's Guide and Deploy in SAP BTP, Kyma Runtime    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-16\nValid as Of: 2024-12-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1734 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhancements to Page Editor\nDescription: When using the Spaces and Pages - New Experience view mode, the following enhancements to the page editor are available:  New buttons on the right side of a section to easily move the sections up and down.   Show/Hide section header.  Context menu for tiles allowing the user to change the size of a tile.  Note  These enhancements are only applicable when creating local pages using the new experience (CDM 3.2 content). \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-16\nValid as Of: 2024-12-16\nVersion: 2412A\n\n--- Record 1735 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Base Theming Content for CF and Neo.\nDescription: The base theming content is updated to version 11.24.0. Review the changes at https://github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-12-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1736 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Appearance dialog\nDescription: Assign themes and theme sets to the UI theme designer using the new Appearance dialog. To access it, go to the user menu and select Appearance.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-12-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1737 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Booster to Set Up SAP Advanced Financial Closing More Easily\nDescription: A booster for the setup of SAP Advanced Financial Closing is now available in the SAP BTP cockpit. By automating several steps, this booster supports you in setting up SAP Advanced Financial Closing and establishing the connection to an SAP S/4HANA Cloud system.  More information:  Automated Setup  Area affected: Solution setup\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-02\nValid as Of: 2024-12-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1738 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deletion of Change Logs Upon Task List Deletion\nDescription: As previously announced, a new system behavior has been implemented for the case of task list template or task list deletion. For compliance reasons, change logs relating to a task list template or task list that is being deleted, are now deleted as well.  Additionally, for change logs relating to task list templates and task lists that had already been removed, a cleanup has taken place to ensure that these change logs are deleted.  More information:  How to Delete Task List Templates and Task Lists  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  Change Log  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-02\nValid as Of: 2024-12-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1739\",1330\n363,\" Task list generation is possible.    A consistency check for all templates will automatically be triggered when this enhancement is released, and the status will be set accordingly.  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  Action: In preparation for this upcoming change, you can already check your task list templates for assignments of deleted users in roles that would cause the consistency checks to fail. This way, you can prevent the consistency checks from failing after the release of this enhancement. To check for such assignments, do the following:  In your task list template, check the assignments on header level for deleted users:  Still on header level, go to Tasks.  In the corresponding user assignment columns, check for the value ***. This will show you users who have been deleted.    In the Closing Structure table of your task list template, do the same to check assignments on folder level.  \nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-21\nValid as Of: 2024-04-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3057 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deletion of Back-End Data\nDescription: When you delete task list templates or task lists referring to on-premise systems, the affected data is marked for deletion in the corresponding communication system. The final deletion, however, is managed by the communication system based on the ILM configuration. This deletion in turn can happen only for data that has been marked for deletion.Note  Your on-premise communication system needs to fulfill specific requirements for the Marked for Deletion indicator to be available. If these requirements are not met and the Marked for Deletion indicator accordingly isn't available, SAP Advanced Financial Closing will keep a reference to the data until the communication system fulfills the requirements and the data can be marked for deletion.For more information about the requirements, see System-Dependent Feature Availability.  More information:  How to Delete Task List Templates and Task Lists  System-Dependent Feature Availability    App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  Action: If you're using SAP Advanced Financial Closing with a connected on-premise system, check whether your communication system fulfills the requirements to mark data used by SAP Advanced Financial Closing for deletion.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-05\nValid as Of: 2024-04-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3058 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional Generate Task List Option\nDescription: You can now generate a task list using the new Generate Task List button on the header of a task list template. It's still possible to generate a task list from the Templates tab.  More information:  How to Generate and Release Task Lists  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-05\nValid as Of: 2024-04-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3059 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Business Feature Validation\nDescription: If tasks in an on-premise communication system are assigned to a business feature (switch) in the communication system, the state of this business feature is now also checked when you copy a task list template.  If the current business feature state renders a task invalid for the specific use case, the template is copied without the invalid tasks.  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-05\nValid as Of: 2024-04-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3060 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Improvement to Copy Folders Dialog for Organizational Units\nDescription: In the Copy Folders dialog for organizational units, you can now use a quick filter to decide which target organizational units are displayed. You have the following options:  All  Not Existing Below System Folder  Existing Below System Folder    Additionally, a new column shows you whether an organizational unit already exists below the system folder.  More information:  How to Copy Folders  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-05\nValid as Of: 2024-04-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",1330\n421,\" lists that had already been removed, a cleanup has taken place to ensure that these change logs are deleted.  More information:  How to Delete Task List Templates and Task Lists  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  Change Log  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-02\nValid as Of: 2024-12-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1739 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deletion of Communication Systems\nDescription: You can now delete communication systems in SAP Advanced Financial Closing even if they have been synchronized before. The prerequisite for the deletion is that the communication system isn't referenced by any task list template, task list, user role, or company code group.  Corresponding audit and business logs are written upon the deletion.  More information:  How to Delete the Connection to a Communication System  Audit Log Integration    App affected:  Specify Communication Systems\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-02\nValid as Of: 2024-12-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1740 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Editable Columns to Change Task Duration\nDescription: In the Tasks table on folder level, the following three columns have now been introduced:  Duration in Days  Duration in Hours  Duration in Minutes    If the folder is in edit mode, you can edit these values directly in the Tasks table without having to access the task details.  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-02\nValid as Of: 2024-12-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",930\n323,\"--- Record 3411 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: UI Improvements - Automation SDK\nDescription: The Options tab for the Automation SDK has been removed from the UI and is no longer supported.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-19\nValid as Of: 2024-02-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3412 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Inbound Communication: Transport Layer Security (TLS 1.3)\nDescription: ABAP Cloud support transport layer security 1.3 for inbound HTTP and WebSocket RFC connections. TLS 1.3 is supported in addition to TLS 1.2\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-19\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3413 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Inbound Communication: Transport Layer Security (TLS 1.3)\nDescription: ABAP Cloud support transport layer security 1.3 for inbound HTTP and WebSocket RFC connections. TLS 1.3 is supported in addition to TLS 1.2